Source: lys-power
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Build-Depends:
 debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/stubbedev/lys/tree/main/power
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/stubbedev/lys.git
Vcs-Browser: https://github.com/stubbedev/lys/tree/main/power

Package: lys-power
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 systemd
Description: adaptive battery charging and power profile policy for the lys desktop
 lys-power holds a laptop's battery at 75-80% while it is plugged in and
 learns when the charger usually comes out, charging to 100% in the two
 hours before that moment. It also sets the power profile itself, the
 ACPI platform profile and the CPUs' energy preference, on every AC edge:
 performance on AC, power-saver on battery. It does not start beside
 power-profiles-daemon or tuned-ppd, which set the same knobs.
 .
 As a user service, lys-power-brightness sets the screen brightness from
 an ambient light sensor, or else from short camera captures that are
 never kept or sent anywhere.
 .
 When lys-shell's idle policy asks, the lys-power-attention user service,
 started over D-Bus, checks with one short camera capture whether a face
 is turned to the screen before it dims; the frames are never kept or
 sent anywhere either.
 .
 The package enables nothing: start the system service with
 systemctl enable --now lys-power, and automatic brightness with
 systemctl --user enable --now lys-power-brightness.
